[{:db/id "q-340589/selection/aee0ed36d5f27e5c51d379777cec01aa4b9d9d1d21633efd06df2ec6a7734965" :answer/id #uuid "54881899-a54c-5639-b946-26bf0330b188" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2$ days" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340589/selection/0079c8a48beca2bf10842552b35e446bd50b97fc1f6836a68f8b517cdc2712b2" :answer/id #uuid "204d3fac-aaf8-55c8-bec6-c76e2300150c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$6$ days" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340589/selection/e820208b3107b9ff83c6bdfe9683306e033310fbfed44ea04cd7a7846296b981" :answer/id #uuid "69d6973f-b2aa-50a2-b0cd-c3507f337e57" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$8$ days" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340589/selection/825c86f8b891916ce4643a0236b11dc2e246eea90f7979eb57a76a4b6a2af84f" :answer/id #uuid "3a84082f-c4b4-570d-9b66-a621cf326595" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$3$ days" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340589/selection/ed212fc7ddc6d13c9ce16adb1e8c2915c4951b56faa6f774e3afdc6ce376b95b" :answer/id #uuid "a3228e04-03c5-5a44-bed9-74f7f5973017" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$9$ days" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340589/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1407b21c-3593-5bf9-b78a-74ff78175b10" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-340589/selection/aee0ed36d5f27e5c51d379777cec01aa4b9d9d1d21633efd06df2ec6a7734965" :answer-field/choices ["q-340589/selection/aee0ed36d5f27e5c51d379777cec01aa4b9d9d1d21633efd06df2ec6a7734965" "q-340589/selection/0079c8a48beca2bf10842552b35e446bd50b97fc1f6836a68f8b517cdc2712b2" "q-340589/selection/e820208b3107b9ff83c6bdfe9683306e033310fbfed44ea04cd7a7846296b981" "q-340589/selection/825c86f8b891916ce4643a0236b11dc2e246eea90f7979eb57a76a4b6a2af84f" "q-340589/selection/ed212fc7ddc6d13c9ce16adb1e8c2915c4951b56faa6f774e3afdc6ce376b95b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-340589" :question/id #uuid "5f6bdeb7-1079-54d3-b26a-5b089c222d68" :question/math-academy-id "q-340589" :question/problem "The rate at which the population of yeast cells in a laboratory culture grows $Y(t),$ after $t$ days, can be modeled by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}Y}{\\text{d}t}=0.55Y.\n$$\n\nHow many days does it take for the population to triple? Round your answer to the nearest day." :question/worked-solution "We model the population growth using the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}Y}{\\text{d}t}=0.55Y.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nY(t)={Y}_{0}\\,{e}^{0.55t},\n$$\n\nwhere ${Y}_{0}$ is the initial population.\n\nLet ${t}_{1}$ be the time when the population is triple the initial number. That is,\n\n$$\nY({t}_{1})=3{Y}_{0}.\n$$\n\nWe solve the above equation for ${t}_{1},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Y({t}_{1}) & ={Y}_{0}{e}^{0.55{t}_{1}} \\\\ 3{Y}_{0} & ={Y}_{0}{e}^{0.55{t}_{1}} \\\\ 3 & ={e}^{0.55{t}_{1}} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡3 & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{0.55{t}_{1}}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡3 & =0.55{t}_{1} \\\\ {t}_{1} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{0.55} \\\\ {t}_{1} & ≈1.997\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRounding to the nearest integer, we conclude that it takes $2$ days for the population to triple." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-340589/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3fcd243-71c6-56d2-9b1b-700f2cd11ac6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-340589"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-340627/selection/25c134856b6f480c826abf6a46dff3c28385a8cd02c79e946038ad307ce2e5d5" :answer/id #uuid "df1a43c5-d989-54f2-bf0e-f4f864da4833" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$7.7$ years" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340627/selection/ffd49047ff447eded16e0c618c5c46f6b627522d9e495463a66ebf860c3a3b7c" :answer/id #uuid "0589410a-8d02-5e42-888d-ce2a5d560a84" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2.5$ years" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340627/selection/d80f2eaa83b259650205bd8ec0cf0d4722ee62a5b7b17b661282e0c5c78aae81" :answer/id #uuid "e9ff4472-ca12-5bf3-a3e1-e761f5ac932c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$3.1$ years" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340627/selection/4a6757e6b4404d31e1b3fce3e3cbed6714ead4c72951fbf516318924ea506aca" :answer/id #uuid "f666ef57-60f0-54e0-aeab-4553baf66e1f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$4.2$ years" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340627/selection/b6b8919febb64cc92a7cf7d8ed4d39a00e73b3521fcc55c836b113f1988aac98" :answer/id #uuid "590ffd50-0e4c-5a07-9717-3beeb7723f55" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2.3$ years" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340627/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6118e46a-5c5c-51ac-8ea3-abd49bc90a7e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-340627/selection/4a6757e6b4404d31e1b3fce3e3cbed6714ead4c72951fbf516318924ea506aca" :answer-field/choices ["q-340627/selection/25c134856b6f480c826abf6a46dff3c28385a8cd02c79e946038ad307ce2e5d5" "q-340627/selection/ffd49047ff447eded16e0c618c5c46f6b627522d9e495463a66ebf860c3a3b7c" "q-340627/selection/d80f2eaa83b259650205bd8ec0cf0d4722ee62a5b7b17b661282e0c5c78aae81" "q-340627/selection/4a6757e6b4404d31e1b3fce3e3cbed6714ead4c72951fbf516318924ea506aca" "q-340627/selection/b6b8919febb64cc92a7cf7d8ed4d39a00e73b3521fcc55c836b113f1988aac98"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-340627" :question/id #uuid "7cff2abe-4fb8-5bec-8737-031cabfdd6ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-340627" :question/problem "The rate at which the cultivated area of a particular region grows $A(t),$ after $t$ years, can be modeled by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=0.08A.\n$$\n\nHow many years does it take for the cultivated area to increase by $40%?$ Round your answer to the nearest decimal place." :question/worked-solution "We model the growth of the cultivated area using the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=0.08A.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nA(t)={A}_{0}\\,{e}^{0.08t},\n$$\n\nwhere ${A}_{0}$ is the initial cultivated area.\n\nLet ${t}_{1}$ be the time when the cultivated area has increased by $40%.$ That is,\n\n$$\nA({t}_{1})=1.4{A}_{0}.\n$$\n\nWe solve the above equation for ${t}_{1},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A({t}_{1}) & ={A}_{0}{e}^{0.08\\cdot {t}_{1}} \\\\ 1.4{A}_{0} & ={A}_{0}{e}^{0.08{t}_{1}} \\\\ 1.4 & ={e}^{0.08{t}_{1}} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(1.4) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{0.08{t}_{1}}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(1.4) & =0.08{t}_{1} \\\\ {t}_{1} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1.4)}{0.08} \\\\ {t}_{1} & ≈4.205\\,9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRounding to the nearest decimal place, we conclude that it takes $4.2$ years for the cultivated area to increase by $40%.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-340627/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3fcd243-71c6-56d2-9b1b-700f2cd11ac6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-340627"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-340590/selection/3164fdde722014ea9e2da2950033c7465c6b13fee2174ec3d73a1331a0ff253a" :answer/id #uuid "b904d403-ada7-5a0e-adda-aef9ed57399f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$4$ years" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340590/selection/290e2822f54af8e34f120802cc911af7630bb6402f8a3d2af65434f5f855bf06" :answer/id #uuid "3dab4e65-2954-51d0-970d-3cb9f9814b56" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$6$ years" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340590/selection/b173e31428e3761a5ad18fe1cc027c5ecd595c6fa6697e8a155ce7309eb3b963" :answer/id #uuid "b53f21dd-3f1b-5fed-afd2-52caa8ef4f31" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$5$ years" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340590/selection/6cc6b9f5e23ab6ced66d0b3e82cb0d9fc6d4256f83b0337d110412234a5cf279" :answer/id #uuid "19af726d-92f9-5c81-9c19-2443ae32a2f3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$3$ years" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340590/selection/8fa5c81f08795dc0fc058766b454fdfcfb72317769aebd1471d94507819b83c0" :answer/id #uuid "ce56bc40-31e3-536a-8287-7f9ed0025523" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2$ years" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340590/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b57d4f66-d561-5057-b00e-13d0a49edace" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-340590/selection/6cc6b9f5e23ab6ced66d0b3e82cb0d9fc6d4256f83b0337d110412234a5cf279" :answer-field/choices ["q-340590/selection/3164fdde722014ea9e2da2950033c7465c6b13fee2174ec3d73a1331a0ff253a" "q-340590/selection/290e2822f54af8e34f120802cc911af7630bb6402f8a3d2af65434f5f855bf06" "q-340590/selection/b173e31428e3761a5ad18fe1cc027c5ecd595c6fa6697e8a155ce7309eb3b963" "q-340590/selection/6cc6b9f5e23ab6ced66d0b3e82cb0d9fc6d4256f83b0337d110412234a5cf279" "q-340590/selection/8fa5c81f08795dc0fc058766b454fdfcfb72317769aebd1471d94507819b83c0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-340590" :question/id #uuid "650d5288-3ff5-5a26-b0f1-c9e721ddc977" :question/math-academy-id "q-340590" :question/problem "The rate at which the number of independent mobile applications on a digital marketplace grows $A(t),$ after $t$ years, can be modeled by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=0.35A.\n$$\n\nHow many years does it take for the number of applications to triple? Round your answer to the nearest year." :question/worked-solution "We model the growth in the number of applications using the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=0.35A.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nA(t)={A}_{0}\\,{e}^{0.35t},\n$$\n\nwhere ${A}_{0}$ is the initial number of applications.\n\nLet ${t}_{1}$ be the time when the number of applications is triple the initial number. That is,\n\n$$\nA({t}_{1})=3{A}_{0}.\n$$\n\nWe solve the above equation for ${t}_{1},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A({t}_{1}) & ={A}_{0}{e}^{0.35{t}_{1}} \\\\ 3{A}_{0} & ={A}_{0}{e}^{0.35{t}_{1}} \\\\ 3 & ={e}^{0.35{t}_{1}} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡3 & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{0.35{t}_{1}}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡3 & =0.35{t}_{1} \\\\ {t}_{1} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{0.35} \\\\ {t}_{1} & ≈3.139\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRounding to the nearest integer, we conclude that it takes $3$ years for the number of applications to triple." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-340590/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3fcd243-71c6-56d2-9b1b-700f2cd11ac6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-340590"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-339289"] :question/problem "The rate at which the population of a particular country grows $P(t),$ after $t$ years, can be modeled by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}=0.02P.\n$$\n\nHow many years does it take for the population to double? Round your answer to the nearest year." :question/worked-solution "We model the population growth using the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}=0.02P.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nP(t)={P}_{0}\\,{e}^{0.02t},\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{0}$ is the initial population.\n\nLet ${t}_{1}$ be the time when the population of the country is double the initial number. That is,\n\n$$\nP({t}_{1})=2{P}_{0}.\n$$\n\nWe solve the above equation for ${t}_{1},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P({t}_{1}) & ={P}_{0}{e}^{0.02\\cdot {t}_{1}} \\\\ 2{P}_{0} & ={P}_{0}{e}^{0.02{t}_{1}} \\\\ 2 & ={e}^{0.02{t}_{1}} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡2 & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{0.02{t}_{1}}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡2 & =0.02{t}_{1} \\\\ {t}_{1} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{0.02} \\\\ {t}_{1} & ≈34.657\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRounding to the nearest integer, we conclude that it takes $35$ years for the population to double." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-340560/selection/85f23a53be0e95a7e191561cc5a77501369717526aae5254cc8d13ed8080d997" :answer/id #uuid "3f492ca8-ea13-59d0-8320-2e74ecc15f19" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "52" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340560/selection/56c57502ed9362f3f416b4398e79545a0252f6594946b2d60ff940ea8bef1e7b" :answer/id #uuid "3b4bf58c-1734-503d-bc33-9204c8c95d1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "44" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340560/selection/4b741b651b6f24cd7370ee85fd4c2dd5b1d9bdb7c612965a77adc26bd59b4a9a" :answer/id #uuid "b97c1c1b-4d13-5cfc-97da-e6f6340889b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "41" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340560/selection/2671fdc3a44bd3421ded09be4e881743067a96eb4e584e442a30f737593eae71" :answer/id #uuid "99c619a9-f8e7-5ced-adbd-7bd2d24ba835" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "38" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340560/selection/30d87289ce9cf4ee21b8a2dd0c77a8f827960a63af81df54e0fe73dfc1b823fc" :answer/id #uuid "f56e05ce-e2ee-53cf-936a-614ecb385f65" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "47" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340560/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fb94e7a9-c401-5f27-81f2-530a753139e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-340560/selection/56c57502ed9362f3f416b4398e79545a0252f6594946b2d60ff940ea8bef1e7b" :answer-field/choices ["q-340560/selection/85f23a53be0e95a7e191561cc5a77501369717526aae5254cc8d13ed8080d997" "q-340560/selection/56c57502ed9362f3f416b4398e79545a0252f6594946b2d60ff940ea8bef1e7b" "q-340560/selection/4b741b651b6f24cd7370ee85fd4c2dd5b1d9bdb7c612965a77adc26bd59b4a9a" "q-340560/selection/2671fdc3a44bd3421ded09be4e881743067a96eb4e584e442a30f737593eae71" "q-340560/selection/30d87289ce9cf4ee21b8a2dd0c77a8f827960a63af81df54e0fe73dfc1b823fc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-340560" :question/id #uuid "982ed208-e355-5a90-b941-1b6ff05c7454" :question/math-academy-id "q-340560" :question/problem "The rate at which the price of a particular product changes $P(t),$ after $t$ years, is given by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}=0.042P.\n$$\n\nIf the price today is $$120,$ how many years will it take for the price to increase to $$750?$\nRound your answer to the nearest year." :question/worked-solution "We model the price growth using the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}=0.042P.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nP(t)={P}_{0}\\,{e}^{0.042t},\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{0}$ is the initial value.\n\nWe're told that the price today is $$120,$ so we have ${P}_{0}=120.$\n\nTherefore, the price $P$ of the product after $t$ years is\n\n$$\nP(t)=120\\,{e}^{0.042t}\\,.\n$$\n\nTo find how many years it takes for the price to grow to $$750,$ we substitute $P(t)=750$ into the equation above and solve for $t,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}750 & =120\\,{e}^{0.042t} \\\\ \\frac{750}{120} & ={e}^{0.042t} \\\\ {e}^{0.042t} & =\\frac{25}{4} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{0.042t}) & =ln\\,(\\frac{25}{4}) \\\\ 0.042t & =ln\\,(\\frac{25}{4}) \\\\ t & =\\frac{1}{0.042}ln\\,(\\frac{25}{4}) \\\\ t & ≈43.633\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRounding to the nearest integer, we conclude that it takes $44$ years for the price to increase to $$750.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-340560/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3fcd243-71c6-56d2-9b1b-700f2cd11ac6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-340560"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-340837/selection/3c6d1b0fd6d36657fe1c8ca4b793e3baa839a43d7518771923fe8ce57c877cd4" :answer/id #uuid "05e03ecf-05b0-5600-b527-c2a42c1e1ae6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$9$ seconds" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340837/selection/dd6c654d0227d6a78e21f1cbd47ebda76a51916f99f8ee70079c936599640ef3" :answer/id #uuid "199fe34b-d8c1-5974-a53f-002c3b369a47" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$12$ seconds" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340837/selection/82a96b3d0b0a22c83448bbb6a66c07b97db8d49bf48c105464b44aabb2903d25" :answer/id #uuid "92d0fac6-046f-5227-9ef8-9dd30d5a88c5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$5$ seconds" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340837/selection/dd0445509d7e1bb04157a8dc79c5f35d89414cfb1a9174c31ea501ca7cd86245" :answer/id #uuid "8b914939-e315-5671-9a86-96c5c6509dbf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$7$ seconds" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340837/selection/9f7b14478cfb591d6455c00c75b134f4372e3b03216b49d772038409797c8161" :answer/id #uuid "10a7fda7-2e7c-5a97-b4ec-b4ea1282cc78" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$15$ seconds" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340837/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "028480f5-0141-5235-8aca-ae2535c9ecc4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-340837/selection/3c6d1b0fd6d36657fe1c8ca4b793e3baa839a43d7518771923fe8ce57c877cd4" :answer-field/choices ["q-340837/selection/3c6d1b0fd6d36657fe1c8ca4b793e3baa839a43d7518771923fe8ce57c877cd4" "q-340837/selection/dd6c654d0227d6a78e21f1cbd47ebda76a51916f99f8ee70079c936599640ef3" "q-340837/selection/82a96b3d0b0a22c83448bbb6a66c07b97db8d49bf48c105464b44aabb2903d25" "q-340837/selection/dd0445509d7e1bb04157a8dc79c5f35d89414cfb1a9174c31ea501ca7cd86245" "q-340837/selection/9f7b14478cfb591d6455c00c75b134f4372e3b03216b49d772038409797c8161"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-340837" :question/id #uuid "810a12d9-d044-5bce-b3d6-cf6256a5234a" :question/math-academy-id "q-340837" :question/problem "A balloon is being deflated. The rate at which the diameter of the balloon decays $D(t),$ after $t$ seconds, can be modeled by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t}=-0.20D.\n$$\n\nHow long does it take for the balloon’s diameter to reduce to $15%$ of its original diameter?  Round your answer to the nearest second." :question/worked-solution "We model the diameter of the balloon using the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t}=-0.20D.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nD(t)={D}_{0}\\,{e}^{-0.20t},\n$$\n\nwhere ${D}_{0}$ is the initial diameter.\n\nLet ${t}_{1}$ be the time when the diameter of the balloon is $15%$ of its original diameter. That is,\n\n$$\nD({t}_{1})=0.15{D}_{0}.\n$$\n\nWe solve the above equation for ${t}_{1},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.15{D}_{0} & ={D}_{0}\\,{e}^{-0.20{t}_{1}} \\\\ 0.15 & ={e}^{-0.20{t}_{1}} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.15) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{-0.20{t}_{1}}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.15) & =-0.20{t}_{1} \\\\ {t}_{1} & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.15)}{0.20} \\\\ {t}_{1} & ≈9.486\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRounding to the nearest second, we conclude that it takes $9$ seconds for the balloon’s diameter to be $15%$ of its original diameter." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-340837/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aa725153-856c-511e-8bbe-7a63286c2994"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-340837"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-340691/selection/1f0c7287d29574b74e984cd714cded7715dd23dc5f107a8e721460544c1c3e74" :answer/id #uuid "e586fdc9-4857-5510-ab6a-7af970785f02" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$12$ minutes" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340691/selection/f49dcfddbf97ffa32dd2fd1623a03947f9e39257e67d73836b51071a44cbf33e" :answer/id #uuid "37b67c09-2b58-5660-91dd-4eed3018c1d9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$20$ minutes" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340691/selection/4553ce3360d7bca80ada8941b775fec541a2fe41cb10d15baac1a85e76ebd820" :answer/id #uuid "7af6d728-8e07-5da8-b552-3f7ac548f63d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$8$ minutes" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340691/selection/a89238ce5bdc1f8b4ac286d734141252f63c68a8a22fd372c5838774152a4f34" :answer/id #uuid "f5846e49-a3f8-5c48-a2b6-d956ab8e10ec" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$6$ minutes" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340691/selection/3d077c0b976c9d8591d5d55657a787353d2ff130dd6146ad78c2c05f20fedd91" :answer/id #uuid "7134a2bd-5e23-50cf-a75c-eb9627ff681a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$15$ minutes" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340691/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "088006b6-6f61-5dce-900e-d7da50500335" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-340691/selection/1f0c7287d29574b74e984cd714cded7715dd23dc5f107a8e721460544c1c3e74" :answer-field/choices ["q-340691/selection/1f0c7287d29574b74e984cd714cded7715dd23dc5f107a8e721460544c1c3e74" "q-340691/selection/f49dcfddbf97ffa32dd2fd1623a03947f9e39257e67d73836b51071a44cbf33e" "q-340691/selection/4553ce3360d7bca80ada8941b775fec541a2fe41cb10d15baac1a85e76ebd820" "q-340691/selection/a89238ce5bdc1f8b4ac286d734141252f63c68a8a22fd372c5838774152a4f34" "q-340691/selection/3d077c0b976c9d8591d5d55657a787353d2ff130dd6146ad78c2c05f20fedd91"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-340691" :question/id #uuid "f2af16ce-2cfd-5b65-bea9-d42294a55eb0" :question/math-academy-id "q-340691" :question/problem "A database is being scanned by cleanup software. The rate at which the number of unprocessed records decays $R(t),$ after $t$ minutes, can be modeled by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}R}{\\text{d}t}=-0.25R.\n$$\n\nIf there are $20\\,000$ unprocessed records at the start of the scan, how many minutes does it take for the number of unprocessed records to decrease to $1\\,000?$ Round your answer to the nearest minute." :question/worked-solution "We model the number of unprocessed records using the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}R}{\\text{d}t}=-0.25R.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nR(t)={R}_{0}\\,{e}^{-0.25t},\n$$\n\nwhere ${R}_{0}$ is the initial number of unprocessed records.\n\nWe're told that there are $20\\,000$ unprocessed records at the start of the scan, so we have ${R}_{0}=20\\,000.$\n\nLet ${t}_{1}$ be the time when the number of unprocessed records has decreased to $1\\,000.$ That is,\n\n$$\nR({t}_{1})=1\\,000.\n$$\n\nWe solve the above equation for ${t}_{1},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1\\,000 & =20\\,000{e}^{-0.25{t}_{1}} \\\\ \\frac{1\\,000}{20\\,000} & ={e}^{-0.25{t}_{1}} \\\\ 0.05 & ={e}^{-0.25{t}_{1}} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.05) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{-0.25{t}_{1}}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.05) & =-0.25{t}_{1} \\\\ {t}_{1} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.05)}{-0.25} \\\\ {t}_{1} & ≈11.982\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRounding to the nearest integer, we conclude that it takes $12$ minutes for the number of unprocessed records to decrease to $1\\,000.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-340691/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aa725153-856c-511e-8bbe-7a63286c2994"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-340691"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-340839/selection/aa68850a3ccd194e01a62abd895c8c51e59abb8c28f5ebfd7d06b999a8280aa0" :answer/id #uuid "12e5cc06-a55a-50e6-85be-d26ae19efa0b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$12$ months" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340839/selection/1d27ab3e3e480ff9c8acdb635960d52d264937915f7c7289410fab118aa1983c" :answer/id #uuid "0397622c-39ee-5760-a2c1-01473280e78e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$75$ months" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340839/selection/560216e41a2fdb6e5d583af667f951db169f5f0b8fdb5977bf52a9586a9a4ea8" :answer/id #uuid "a4664441-7cd9-58f5-8d5b-1cccb6dcf774" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$25$ months" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340839/selection/5971a8c99e7c8de605d29311077a56f02b7d2c238f0dbee45cba2f4df9c1cc0f" :answer/id #uuid "61ce5e50-f312-5904-8fbf-462580422a80" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$3$ months" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340839/selection/0b2010ea4b1180f40d063410b04c3d4ec545d6e6b059e78295a155e803ce2f78" :answer/id #uuid "a3768b2b-e6b2-5fa2-9cfc-b2b723637074" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$6$ months" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340839/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e1ee6832-3fd9-5359-bbf2-55128a903aa0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-340839/selection/aa68850a3ccd194e01a62abd895c8c51e59abb8c28f5ebfd7d06b999a8280aa0" :answer-field/choices ["q-340839/selection/aa68850a3ccd194e01a62abd895c8c51e59abb8c28f5ebfd7d06b999a8280aa0" "q-340839/selection/1d27ab3e3e480ff9c8acdb635960d52d264937915f7c7289410fab118aa1983c" "q-340839/selection/560216e41a2fdb6e5d583af667f951db169f5f0b8fdb5977bf52a9586a9a4ea8" "q-340839/selection/5971a8c99e7c8de605d29311077a56f02b7d2c238f0dbee45cba2f4df9c1cc0f" "q-340839/selection/0b2010ea4b1180f40d063410b04c3d4ec545d6e6b059e78295a155e803ce2f78"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-340839" :question/id #uuid "e95d42fb-17c7-5032-aeb8-e1c39a0b2c28" :question/math-academy-id "q-340839" :question/problem "The amount of charge stored in a battery is decreasing due to self-discharge. The rate at which the amount of stored charge decays $W(t),$ after $t$ months, can be modeled by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}W}{\\text{d}t}=-0.025W.\n$$\n\nHow long does it take for the amount of stored charge to be $75%$ of the original amount? Round your answer to the nearest month." :question/worked-solution "We model the amount of stored charge using the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}W}{\\text{d}t}=-0.025W.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nW(t)={W}_{0}\\,{e}^{-0.025t},\n$$\n\nwhere ${W}_{0}$ is the initial stored charge.\n\nLet ${t}_{1}$ be the time when the amount of stored charge is $75%$ of the original amount. That is,\n\n$$\nW({t}_{1})=0.75{W}_{0}.\n$$\n\nWe solve the above equation for ${t}_{1},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.75{W}_{0} & ={W}_{0}\\,{e}^{-0.025{t}_{1}} \\\\ 0.75 & ={e}^{-0.025{t}_{1}} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.75) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{-0.025{t}_{1}}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.75) & =-0.025{t}_{1} \\\\ {t}_{1} & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.75)}{0.025} \\\\ {t}_{1} & ≈11.507\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRounding to the nearest month, we conclude that it takes $12$ months for the amount of stored charge to be $75%$ of the original amount." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-340839/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aa725153-856c-511e-8bbe-7a63286c2994"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-340839"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-339321"] :question/problem "The rate at which the number of particles in a radioactive substance decays $N(t),$ after $t$ years, can be modeled by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=-0.01N.\n$$\n\nHow many years will it take for the number of particles to be $1%$ of the original number? Round your answer to the nearest year." :question/worked-solution "We model the number of particles using the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=-0.01N.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nN(t)={N}_{0}\\,{e}^{-0.01t},\n$$\n\nwhere ${N}_{0}$ is the initial number of particles.\n\nLet ${t}_{1}$ be the time when the number of particles is $1%$ of its initial number. That is,\n\n$$\nN({t}_{1})=0.01{N}_{0}.\n$$\n\nWe solve the above equation for ${t}_{1},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.01{N}_{0} & ={N}_{0}\\,{e}^{-0.01{t}_{1}} \\\\ 0.01 & ={e}^{-0.01{t}_{1}} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.01) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{-0.01{t}_{1}}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.01) & =-0.01{t}_{1} \\\\ {t}_{1} & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.01)}{0.01} \\\\ {t}_{1} & ≈460.517\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRounding to the nearest integer, we conclude that it takes $461$ years for the number of particles to be $1%$ of the original number." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-340695/selection/bc99f3bfde4861294054eb6589df61db5f5d62481cb0007ef272ccce91598ac9" :answer/id #uuid "4d8f8d56-e5ed-5630-97be-5d4b2ee23df2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$12$ weeks" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340695/selection/8645a251fab0da0470508c26bcf280658de54453c6d4f77e3fa09e928334c29e" :answer/id #uuid "3452282a-4e4e-55cc-a748-23bfd64cce7b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$8$ weeks" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340695/selection/3fd91de91b5745e6ba091daa3fbcc207d2c72c23eb095260d83baedbb989f50d" :answer/id #uuid "c824b699-e8fb-5750-920d-e6ba929a6292" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$17$ weeks" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340695/selection/4f0e0e6266619aae6d24f1bb896cf5260f8c24895ec1519637d5375eec22305c" :answer/id #uuid "19126342-60d5-5541-9058-1d89b8a1546c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$20$ weeks" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340695/selection/b4db297e770d4f12d5ec652aaa007251095cac2f3ed0bf9d05b51dd0054a751e" :answer/id #uuid "868cbb1a-4f0b-50fe-a68e-b4192e1f8db3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$25$ weeks" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340695/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "da4ccf10-1528-51c9-832a-f68749c13838" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-340695/selection/3fd91de91b5745e6ba091daa3fbcc207d2c72c23eb095260d83baedbb989f50d" :answer-field/choices ["q-340695/selection/bc99f3bfde4861294054eb6589df61db5f5d62481cb0007ef272ccce91598ac9" "q-340695/selection/8645a251fab0da0470508c26bcf280658de54453c6d4f77e3fa09e928334c29e" "q-340695/selection/3fd91de91b5745e6ba091daa3fbcc207d2c72c23eb095260d83baedbb989f50d" "q-340695/selection/4f0e0e6266619aae6d24f1bb896cf5260f8c24895ec1519637d5375eec22305c" "q-340695/selection/b4db297e770d4f12d5ec652aaa007251095cac2f3ed0bf9d05b51dd0054a751e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-340695" :question/id #uuid "b9919d3f-10c9-53e2-8d3a-e92839556535" :question/math-academy-id "q-340695" :question/problem "The rate at which the number of active users of a mobile app decreases $U(t),$ after $t$ weeks from launch, can be modeled by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}U}{\\text{d}t}=-0.04U.\n$$\n\nIf there are $40\\,000$ active users at launch, how many weeks does it take for the number of active users to decrease to $20\\,000?$  Round your answer to the nearest week." :question/worked-solution "We model the number of active users using the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}U}{\\text{d}t}=-0.04U.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nU(t)={U}_{0}\\,{e}^{-0.04t},\n$$\n\nwhere ${U}_{0}$ is the initial number of active users.\n\nWe're told that there are $40\\,000$ active users at launch, so we have ${U}_{0}=40\\,000.$\n\nLet ${t}_{1}$ be the time when the number of active users has decreased to $20\\,000.$ That is,\n\n$$\nU({t}_{1})=20\\,000.\n$$\n\nWe solve the above equation for ${t}_{1},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}20\\,000 & =40\\,000{e}^{-0.04{t}_{1}} \\\\ \\frac{20\\,000}{40\\,000} & ={e}^{-0.04{t}_{1}} \\\\ 0.5 & ={e}^{-0.04{t}_{1}} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.5) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{-0.04{t}_{1}}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.5) & =-0.04{t}_{1} \\\\ {t}_{1} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.5)}{-0.04} \\\\ {t}_{1} & ≈17.329\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRounding to the nearest integer, we conclude that it takes $17$ weeks for the number of active users to decrease to $20\\,000.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-340695/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aa725153-856c-511e-8bbe-7a63286c2994"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-340695"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-339228/selection/e981d84006ae566e115a2dba8f62a2907c7650728eee1076c64a5764698bbf1c" :answer/id #uuid "6cebfeef-ab71-56ed-920a-238323d1db54" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$7.7$ hours" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339228/selection/e2a4d91d99a9d89005e0bc4357da2eb294099580f6b793a59d4324f3350d09db" :answer/id #uuid "9a3d0e7a-8c8d-5e28-946e-0ce02a291052" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$7.3$ hours" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339228/selection/2d1e0a3cb7fdf88fb873978c63a159e22ec01baeb338a172621477bde19924dc" :answer/id #uuid "970b64b6-3de6-584c-8cef-88ee9baf2c1c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$7.5$ hours" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339228/selection/5b77a3d4617b30d7e0e35157e89c6d744df32a670c0c943d6729160366a232d9" :answer/id #uuid "5868d57c-ddc3-5b86-836a-58c2452d3573" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$7.6$ hours" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339228/selection/2def8f31b637bdf38a7b2545a9e512f48a769d11b650406e867d129fe81f63a6" :answer/id #uuid "b7ce8bda-7a4f-5106-9765-2fa43c090206" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$7.4$ hours" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339228/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ff4a15e7-82ea-573a-8ecc-f14c1e390806" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-339228/selection/5b77a3d4617b30d7e0e35157e89c6d744df32a670c0c943d6729160366a232d9" :answer-field/choices ["q-339228/selection/e981d84006ae566e115a2dba8f62a2907c7650728eee1076c64a5764698bbf1c" "q-339228/selection/e2a4d91d99a9d89005e0bc4357da2eb294099580f6b793a59d4324f3350d09db" "q-339228/selection/2d1e0a3cb7fdf88fb873978c63a159e22ec01baeb338a172621477bde19924dc" "q-339228/selection/5b77a3d4617b30d7e0e35157e89c6d744df32a670c0c943d6729160366a232d9" "q-339228/selection/2def8f31b637bdf38a7b2545a9e512f48a769d11b650406e867d129fe81f63a6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339228" :question/id #uuid "50e0c94d-ecd1-5368-b337-75ee0d290e30" :question/math-academy-id "q-339228" :question/problem "A car is traveling along a straight road to a particular destination. The remaining distance $D(t)$ varies according to the differential equation ${D}^{′}(t)=-rD(t),$ where $t$ is the time, measured in hours, and $r>0.$ Two hours into the journey, the remaining distance is three-quarters of the journey's total distance. How long does it take for the remaining distance to reduce to one-third of the journey's total distance? Round your answer to one decimal place." :question/worked-solution "The general solution to the given differential equation is\n\n$$\nD(t)={D}_{0}{e}^{-rt},\n$$\n\nwhere ${D}_{0}$ is the distance when $t=0.$\n\nLet ${t}_{1}$ be the time when the distance equals $\\frac{1}{3}{D}_{0}.$ Then, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D({t}_{1}) & =\\frac{1}{3}{D}_{0}\\,⇒\\,{D}_{0}{e}^{-r{t}_{1}}=\\frac{1}{3}{D}_{0}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation for ${t}_{1},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{0}{e}^{-r{t}_{1}} & =\\frac{1}{3}{D}_{0} \\\\ \\cancel{{D}_{0}}{e}^{-r{t}_{1}} & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cancel{{D}_{0}} \\\\ {e}^{-r{t}_{1}} & =\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{-r{t}_{1}}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\ -r{t}_{1} & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3 \\\\ {t}_{1} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{r}\\,\\,(∗)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now need to calculate $r.$ We're told that two hours into the journey, the remaining distance is three-quarters of the journey's total distance. Therefore,\n\n$$\nD(2)=\\frac{3}{4}{D}_{0}\\,⇒\\,{D}_{0}{e}^{-2r}=\\frac{3}{4}{D}_{0}.\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation for $r,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{0}{e}^{-2r} & =\\frac{3}{4}{D}_{0} \\\\ \\cancel{{D}_{0}}{e}^{-2r} & =\\frac{3}{4}\\cancel{{D}_{0}} \\\\ {e}^{-2r} & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{-2r}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{4}) \\\\ -2r & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.75) \\\\ r & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.75)}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting this into $(∗)$ and evaluating, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}_{1} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{r} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.75)}{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.75)} \\\\  & ≈7.6,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to one decimal place." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-339228/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ea69de7-f96b-5949-9aec-584cb4e2f214"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-339228"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-339222/selection/8b0b966614095063faa799013e6e97fc544ee578b5b12f1281fd3aa654c5f142" :answer/id #uuid "56bed141-3d00-5c91-88c8-ac4000a6ac14" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$6.4$ weeks" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339222/selection/ba4070d59e0e9a5cc7137156755ef4eddceff06eade5e72f2154867c5a4f102b" :answer/id #uuid "964bf40b-f85c-589d-aecd-3241234bbad7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$6.5$ weeks" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339222/selection/56e8cc6bcb4d154209cb66ee29bee21841abcca6c79ae641f60628e13db3578f" :answer/id #uuid "d608dcfc-e8e8-5d79-bf0b-2a7adb61cd08" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$6.3$ weeks" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339222/selection/bbb635d4a99a36a0436d3019920af6a16671c6851a9509103ee27d08ea336c37" :answer/id #uuid "362af56f-8ea5-5dc1-97b4-d8def6cdd9c8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$6.2$ weeks" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339222/selection/62927cee4510ae1785f58753c1f8f83f20c304d04302dda4b0d6b093c50fb626" :answer/id #uuid "5ea06213-af25-5091-bdf2-8fe0b84576ff" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$6$ weeks" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339222/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "65bad813-2d62-5544-8fb0-4fbea88d6603" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-339222/selection/56e8cc6bcb4d154209cb66ee29bee21841abcca6c79ae641f60628e13db3578f" :answer-field/choices ["q-339222/selection/8b0b966614095063faa799013e6e97fc544ee578b5b12f1281fd3aa654c5f142" "q-339222/selection/ba4070d59e0e9a5cc7137156755ef4eddceff06eade5e72f2154867c5a4f102b" "q-339222/selection/56e8cc6bcb4d154209cb66ee29bee21841abcca6c79ae641f60628e13db3578f" "q-339222/selection/bbb635d4a99a36a0436d3019920af6a16671c6851a9509103ee27d08ea336c37" "q-339222/selection/62927cee4510ae1785f58753c1f8f83f20c304d04302dda4b0d6b093c50fb626"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339222" :question/id #uuid "b562af2b-8343-5000-806c-d01887adea11" :question/math-academy-id "q-339222" :question/problem "The number of subscribers $N(t)$ to an e-learning platform varies according to the differential equation ${N}^{′}(t)=rN(t),$ where $t$ is the time since the platform was launched, measured in weeks, and $r>0.$ It is known that the number of subscribers doubles after the first four weeks. How long does it take for the number of subscribers to triple after the platform is launched? Round your answer to one decimal place." :question/worked-solution "The general solution to the given differential equation is\n\n$$\nN(t)={N}_{0}{e}^{rt},\n$$\n\nwhere ${N}_{0}$ is the number of subscribers when $t=0.$\n\nLet ${t}_{1}$ be the time when the number of subscribers equals $3{N}_{0}.$ Then, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N({t}_{1}) & =3{N}_{0}\\,⇒\\,{N}_{0}{e}^{r{t}_{1}}=3{N}_{0}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation for ${t}_{1},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{N}_{0}{e}^{r{t}_{1}} & =3{N}_{0} \\\\ \\cancel{{N}_{0}}{e}^{r{t}_{1}} & =3\\cancel{{N}_{0}} \\\\ {e}^{r{t}_{1}} & =3 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{r{t}_{1}}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3) \\\\ r{t}_{1} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡3 \\\\ {t}_{1} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{r}\\,\\,(∗)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now need to calculate $r.$ We're told that the number of subscribers doubles after the first four weeks the platform is launched. Therefore,\n\n$$\nN(4)=2{N}_{0}\\,⇒\\,{N}_{0}{e}^{4r}=2{N}_{0}.\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation for $r,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{N}_{0}{e}^{4r} & =2{N}_{0} \\\\ \\cancel{{N}_{0}}{e}^{4r} & =2\\cancel{{N}_{0}} \\\\ {e}^{4r} & =2 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{4r}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2) \\\\ r & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting this into $(∗)$ and evaluating, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}_{1} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{r} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{(\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{4})} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\  & ≈6.3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to one decimal place." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-339222/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ea69de7-f96b-5949-9aec-584cb4e2f214"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-339222"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-339223/selection/961cb5fd97ab856d5c2593ecabe76db36aacca9b610b7406344bb572409978bc" :answer/id #uuid "60a06ac6-57a7-5c79-a806-80dfd750559d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2.5$ months" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339223/selection/ee2f8cf28553bb0df972a8d8ddebe70363e1f0a181239135cfa5a278b0c3680c" :answer/id #uuid "2f921598-f2e2-5117-8d19-388e5cf3201c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2.6$ months" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339223/selection/205c9cbbc30d2aa6e39b01c5cec8ef201815cf040c727c4a267ff61fe3c88dec" :answer/id #uuid "7dac645a-392d-586b-b6d4-83bed8b8229e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2.4$ months" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339223/selection/bb3e6d3f141691031508b9b6f24fd3ad96b62fc42b53a516b69ab03797040f62" :answer/id #uuid "45351659-a55b-5fac-a2ef-df58e98a59cb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2.7$ months" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339223/selection/6ffa8887f7a8aacb071624b837721f053b8e0df329cccbdaee383fbd42374f8a" :answer/id #uuid "7b3bf336-bbbb-5243-8efc-0253c7bec437" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2.8$ months" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339223/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "148274d4-7192-50b3-b493-f396647a6280" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-339223/selection/ee2f8cf28553bb0df972a8d8ddebe70363e1f0a181239135cfa5a278b0c3680c" :answer-field/choices ["q-339223/selection/961cb5fd97ab856d5c2593ecabe76db36aacca9b610b7406344bb572409978bc" "q-339223/selection/ee2f8cf28553bb0df972a8d8ddebe70363e1f0a181239135cfa5a278b0c3680c" "q-339223/selection/205c9cbbc30d2aa6e39b01c5cec8ef201815cf040c727c4a267ff61fe3c88dec" "q-339223/selection/bb3e6d3f141691031508b9b6f24fd3ad96b62fc42b53a516b69ab03797040f62" "q-339223/selection/6ffa8887f7a8aacb071624b837721f053b8e0df329cccbdaee383fbd42374f8a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339223" :question/id #uuid "0c960e16-2c26-5c1d-a148-66f3137714ce" :question/math-academy-id "q-339223" :question/problem "The population $P(t)$ of mice in a forest varies according to the differential equation ${P}^{′}(t)=rP(t),$ where $t$ is the time, measured in months from the start of the observation period, and $r>0.$  It is known that the mouse population quintuples (increases fivefold) after the first two months. How long does it take for the mouse population to increase eightfold from the start of the observation period? Round your answer to one decimal place." :question/worked-solution "The general solution to the given differential equation is\n\n$$\nP(t)={P}_{0}{e}^{rt},\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{0}$ is the mouse population when $t=0.$\n\nLet ${t}_{1}$ be the time when the mouse population equals $8{P}_{0}.$ Then, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P({t}_{1}) & =8{P}_{0}\\,⇒\\,{P}_{0}{e}^{r{t}_{1}}=8{P}_{0}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation for ${t}_{1},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{0}{e}^{r{t}_{1}} & =8{P}_{0} \\\\ \\cancel{{P}_{0}}{e}^{r{t}_{1}} & =8\\cancel{{P}_{0}} \\\\ {e}^{r{t}_{1}} & =8 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{r{t}_{1}}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8) \\\\ r{t}_{1} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡8 \\\\ {t}_{1} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡8}{r}\\,\\,(∗)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now need to calculate $r.$ We're told that the population quintuples after the first two months. Therefore,\n\n$$\nP(2)=5{P}_{0}\\,⇒\\,{P}_{0}{e}^{2r}=5{P}_{0}.\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation for $r,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{0}{e}^{2r} & =5{P}_{0} \\\\ \\cancel{{P}_{0}}{e}^{2r} & =5\\cancel{{P}_{0}} \\\\ {e}^{2r} & =5 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2r}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5) \\\\ r & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting this into $(∗)$ and evaluating, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}_{1} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡8}{r} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡8}{(\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡8}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5} \\\\  & ≈2.6,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to one decimal place." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-339223/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ea69de7-f96b-5949-9aec-584cb4e2f214"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-339223"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-339226/selection/cda4e09f3ca8772f220df0a589ea79b0bb6353de80a5e1f9c4fe92de70271f5e" :answer/id #uuid "2e87dfd0-2a73-5c94-a232-cae0d912f08c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2.1$ years" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339226/selection/6ece2d8ec6a5b9bd9a3bb4f7d480c2ec598da67c532326d348f1a0a944b80df3" :answer/id #uuid "14618948-3ac7-56ac-a9a1-f423307b895b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2.4$ years" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339226/selection/8fa5c81f08795dc0fc058766b454fdfcfb72317769aebd1471d94507819b83c0" :answer/id #uuid "c5613c3f-4f2f-527f-9cfc-5cb3eb50a877" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2$ years" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339226/selection/b6b8919febb64cc92a7cf7d8ed4d39a00e73b3521fcc55c836b113f1988aac98" :answer/id #uuid "c1eeb3c4-6f82-597a-97a7-1bc7534a38be" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2.3$ years" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339226/selection/ffd49047ff447eded16e0c618c5c46f6b627522d9e495463a66ebf860c3a3b7c" :answer/id #uuid "23b8910d-8d0e-555f-b48f-586a7fb16116" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2.5$ years" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339226/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6764520b-2294-54f7-beb2-c00c33af2cfe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-339226/selection/b6b8919febb64cc92a7cf7d8ed4d39a00e73b3521fcc55c836b113f1988aac98" :answer-field/choices ["q-339226/selection/cda4e09f3ca8772f220df0a589ea79b0bb6353de80a5e1f9c4fe92de70271f5e" "q-339226/selection/6ece2d8ec6a5b9bd9a3bb4f7d480c2ec598da67c532326d348f1a0a944b80df3" "q-339226/selection/8fa5c81f08795dc0fc058766b454fdfcfb72317769aebd1471d94507819b83c0" "q-339226/selection/b6b8919febb64cc92a7cf7d8ed4d39a00e73b3521fcc55c836b113f1988aac98" "q-339226/selection/ffd49047ff447eded16e0c618c5c46f6b627522d9e495463a66ebf860c3a3b7c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339226" :question/id #uuid "8375c335-8cf2-5c82-b2c9-770890e7d65a" :question/math-academy-id "q-339226" :question/problem "The value $V(t)$ of a tech device varies according to the differential equation ${V}^{′}(t)=-rV(t),$ where $t$ is the time, measured in years, and $r>0.$ It is known that the value reduces by one-half after the first year. How long does it take for the value to reduce to one-fifth of its original value? Round your answer to one decimal place." :question/worked-solution "The general solution to the given differential equation is\n\n$$\nV(t)={V}_{0}{e}^{-rt},\n$$\n\nwhere ${V}_{0}$ is the value when $t=0.$\n\nLet ${t}_{1}$ be the time when the value equals $\\frac{1}{5}{V}_{0}.$ Then, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V({t}_{1}) & =\\frac{1}{5}{V}_{0}\\,⇒\\,{V}_{0}{e}^{-r{t}_{1}}=\\frac{1}{5}{V}_{0}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation for ${t}_{1},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{V}_{0}{e}^{-r{t}_{1}} & =\\frac{1}{5}{V}_{0} \\\\ \\cancel{{V}_{0}}{e}^{-r{t}_{1}} & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cancel{{V}_{0}} \\\\ {e}^{-r{t}_{1}} & =\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{-r{t}_{1}}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{5}) \\\\ -r{t}_{1} & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5 \\\\ {t}_{1} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{r}\\,\\,(∗)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now need to calculate $r.$ We're told that the value reduces by one-half after the first year. Therefore,\n\n$$\nV(1)=\\frac{1}{2}{V}_{0}\\,⇒\\,{V}_{0}{e}^{-r}=\\frac{1}{2}{V}_{0}.\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation for $r,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{V}_{0}{e}^{-r} & =\\frac{1}{2}{V}_{0} \\\\ \\cancel{{V}_{0}}{e}^{-r} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cancel{{V}_{0}} \\\\ {e}^{-r} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{-r}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\ -r & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\ r & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting this into $(∗)$ and evaluating, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}_{1} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{r} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\  & ≈2.3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to one decimal place." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-339226/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ea69de7-f96b-5949-9aec-584cb4e2f214"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-339226"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-339219/selection/d80f2eaa83b259650205bd8ec0cf0d4722ee62a5b7b17b661282e0c5c78aae81" :answer/id #uuid "be0500a3-7328-511b-852a-2f6318db8d91" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$3.1$ years" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339219/selection/31ef6027c0704b566339aa8b81de92be5f8b795f5d8653b3ea12be58e6e1c802" :answer/id #uuid "93757373-37b2-565d-b77a-94b67f9ae8ea" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$3.4$ years" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339219/selection/df8a46e3144f82eb924813778a674ce8fa9efedefa1e8177a3519f77d1219219" :answer/id #uuid "c10c1c5a-1880-515d-80b1-a3f5a7992098" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$3.2$ years" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339219/selection/e68ad7bb0e4ca013f350295f195c29058e2777505e37e6926ad3fa0f69549f5b" :answer/id #uuid "ac37a07f-891b-52c6-a462-0ff382ad551b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$3.5$ years" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339219/selection/34b2a34c4413f2229040e5779af451b3a8e778df9e56367d7beb59f5e1363166" :answer/id #uuid "bc42a193-a3af-561e-9e07-f437c0c4565e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$3.8$ years" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339219/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1171af75-2fac-56fe-84d4-d4a7aac6dfa0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-339219/selection/34b2a34c4413f2229040e5779af451b3a8e778df9e56367d7beb59f5e1363166" :answer-field/choices ["q-339219/selection/d80f2eaa83b259650205bd8ec0cf0d4722ee62a5b7b17b661282e0c5c78aae81" "q-339219/selection/31ef6027c0704b566339aa8b81de92be5f8b795f5d8653b3ea12be58e6e1c802" "q-339219/selection/df8a46e3144f82eb924813778a674ce8fa9efedefa1e8177a3519f77d1219219" "q-339219/selection/e68ad7bb0e4ca013f350295f195c29058e2777505e37e6926ad3fa0f69549f5b" "q-339219/selection/34b2a34c4413f2229040e5779af451b3a8e778df9e56367d7beb59f5e1363166"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339219" :question/id #uuid "fa8fd170-b6ae-5617-9078-56e4cb7214c2" :question/math-academy-id "q-339219" :question/problem "The price $P(t)$ of a particular good varies according to the differential equation ${P}^{′}(t)=rP(t),$ where $t$ is the time, measured in years, and $r>0.$ It is known that the price of the good tripled after the first six years. How long did it take for the price to double from the initial price?" :question/worked-solution "The general solution to the given differential equation is\n\n$$\nP(t)={P}_{0}{e}^{rt},\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{0}$ is the price of the good when $t=0.$\n\nLet ${t}_{1}$ be the time when the price equals $2{P}_{0}.$ Then, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P({t}_{1}) & =2{P}_{0}\\,⇒\\,{P}_{0}{e}^{r{t}_{1}}=2{P}_{0}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation for ${t}_{1},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{0}{e}^{r{t}_{1}} & =2{P}_{0} \\\\ \\cancel{{P}_{0}}{e}^{r{t}_{1}} & =2\\cancel{{P}_{0}} \\\\ {e}^{r{t}_{1}} & =2 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{r{t}_{1}}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\ r{t}_{1} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\ {t}_{1} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{r}\\,\\,(∗)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now need to calculate $r.$ We're told that the price of the good tripled after the first six years. Therefore,\n\n$$\nP(6)=3{P}_{0}\\,⇒\\,{P}_{0}{e}^{6r}=3{P}_{0}.\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation for $r,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{0}{e}^{6r} & =3{P}_{0} \\\\ \\cancel{{P}_{0}}{e}^{6r} & =3\\cancel{{P}_{0}} \\\\ {e}^{6r} & =3 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{6r}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3) \\\\ r & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting this into $(∗)$ and evaluating, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}_{1} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{r} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{(\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{6})} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\  & ≈3.8,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to one decimal place." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-339219/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ea69de7-f96b-5949-9aec-584cb4e2f214"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-339219"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-339237/selection/656c77a8c01ec15151fc0ad56021c9eff1268721b7c89b847043b057854ce634" :answer/id #uuid "8ef341ee-3472-551a-8395-a4225a8af718" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1\\,986" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339237/selection/4188cbaa094dc2e8755f17ec60aefd913facfa05cf5a39aaeea1c963ef92dc8b" :answer/id #uuid "bbe3966f-020c-52d4-856f-41cb3947e65a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1\\,896" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339237/selection/cad30fee830e09a71877d787178e9dda6bc848451031667916f5fb6ce8854ef0" :answer/id #uuid "cbc45e21-1597-57f1-9e4e-cbf37a3fbfa2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,986" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339237/selection/7c2d23c0f80cb6692394b303ddccea12da0b76afc776afbf0bc708115978f5b0" :answer/id #uuid "342918a5-6945-50d1-a6ca-5896b529c7cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1\\,698" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339237/selection/232e82fca704319468f7991867521693c4170a40774713a867f6878be51cd64c" :answer/id #uuid "2d306403-65b0-57ab-89ae-b5782aad3547" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,869" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339237/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "120fde52-b7d0-5888-8b9f-f6dec687d2d1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-339237/selection/7c2d23c0f80cb6692394b303ddccea12da0b76afc776afbf0bc708115978f5b0" :answer-field/choices ["q-339237/selection/656c77a8c01ec15151fc0ad56021c9eff1268721b7c89b847043b057854ce634" "q-339237/selection/4188cbaa094dc2e8755f17ec60aefd913facfa05cf5a39aaeea1c963ef92dc8b" "q-339237/selection/cad30fee830e09a71877d787178e9dda6bc848451031667916f5fb6ce8854ef0" "q-339237/selection/7c2d23c0f80cb6692394b303ddccea12da0b76afc776afbf0bc708115978f5b0" "q-339237/selection/232e82fca704319468f7991867521693c4170a40774713a867f6878be51cd64c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339237" :question/id #uuid "df12602c-2f6c-5e5c-948b-0aa6a8d760e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-339237" :question/problem "The population $P(t)$ of rabbits in a forest after $t$ weeks can be modeled by the differential equation ${P}^{′}(t)=0.11P(t).$ If there were $786$ rabbits after $8$ weeks, calculate the rabbit population after $15$ weeks." :question/worked-solution "The general solution to the given differential equation is\n\n$$\nP(t)={P}_{0}\\,{e}^{0.11t},\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{0}$ is the initial number of rabbits.\n\nWe are given that after $8$ weeks, there were $786$ rabbits. So, substituting $t=8$ and $P(8)=786$ into our general solution and solving for ${P}_{0},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(8) & ={P}_{0}\\,{e}^{0.11\\cdot 8} \\\\ 786 & ={P}_{0}\\,{e}^{0.88} \\\\ {P}_{0} & =\\frac{786}{{e}^{0.88}} \\\\  & ≈326.019,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.\n\nHence, our particular solution is\n\n$$\nP(t)=326.019\\,{e}^{0.11t}.\n$$\n\nWe want to find the number of rabbits after $15$ weeks. So, substituting $t=15$ into our particular solution, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(15) & =326.019\\,{e}^{0.11\\cdot 15} \\\\  & =326.019\\,{e}^{1.65} \\\\  & ≈1\\,698,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest whole number. \n\nTherefore, there will be about $1\\,698$ rabbits after $15$ weeks." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-339237/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aeeaf85-0cbd-58ab-91d6-93448ff54b4d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-339237"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-339239/selection/761b6711a18b0c6830edfa9dd851899391f7d4bdbacc567f786e28ebecea7bcb" :answer/id #uuid "22717357-976d-51f0-b88e-265401ec0e69" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14\\,257" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339239/selection/a618824396664cbb41dbc639d8c17c74d848eea85bdf59a09c33f30687ee43c7" :answer/id #uuid "bad84617-8ac1-546f-9d83-a6691d8f8bb2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14\\,542" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339239/selection/9227fa99f492f0b1d6e9b9ba08061ed4a16b77192edc8f12e36c3926e590f8ec" :answer/id #uuid "47770667-4e39-5080-8a3e-093761f1dd56" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "17\\,542" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339239/selection/266e17687ddb7852435caefd6b14c20639eea929651a0e909cfee60456eeca1f" :answer/id #uuid "96d5056b-2381-5c59-9e5a-0dc070dcc453" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12\\,547" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339239/selection/2f2f34f9524934d1c07e0bd33251c02478ca8660d2f4216fccae66957ae826b0" :answer/id #uuid "6dfdd65d-d9ca-5787-a537-f31f96aba869" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15\\,247" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339239/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "92dd5fbe-3bce-5bb4-a77f-c29eae9a960c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-339239/selection/266e17687ddb7852435caefd6b14c20639eea929651a0e909cfee60456eeca1f" :answer-field/choices ["q-339239/selection/761b6711a18b0c6830edfa9dd851899391f7d4bdbacc567f786e28ebecea7bcb" "q-339239/selection/a618824396664cbb41dbc639d8c17c74d848eea85bdf59a09c33f30687ee43c7" "q-339239/selection/9227fa99f492f0b1d6e9b9ba08061ed4a16b77192edc8f12e36c3926e590f8ec" "q-339239/selection/266e17687ddb7852435caefd6b14c20639eea929651a0e909cfee60456eeca1f" "q-339239/selection/2f2f34f9524934d1c07e0bd33251c02478ca8660d2f4216fccae66957ae826b0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339239" :question/id #uuid "6b39468d-5d98-5128-aa1e-9a26b817cf16" :question/math-academy-id "q-339239" :question/problem "The population $P(t)$ of fish in a pond after $t$ weeks can be modeled by the differential equation ${P}^{′}(t)=0.09P(t).$ If the fish population was $8\\,000$ after $18$ weeks, calculate the fish population after $23$ weeks." :question/worked-solution "The general solution to the given differential equation is\n\n$$\nP(t)={P}_{0}\\,{e}^{0.09t},\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{0}$ is the initial fish population.\n\nWe are given that after $18$ weeks, the population was $8\\,000.$ So, substituting $t=18$ and $P(18)=8\\,000$ into our general solution and solving for ${P}_{0},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(18) & ={P}_{0}\\,{e}^{0.09\\cdot 18} \\\\ 8\\,000 & ={P}_{0}\\,{e}^{1.62} \\\\ {P}_{0} & =\\frac{8\\,000}{{e}^{1.62}} \\\\  & ≈1\\,583.190,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.\n\nHence, our particular solution is\n\n$$\nP(t)=1\\,583.190\\,{e}^{0.09t}.\n$$\n\nWe want to find the fish population after $23$ weeks. So, substituting $t=23$ into our particular solution, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(23) & =1\\,583.190\\,{e}^{0.09\\cdot 23} \\\\  & =1\\,583.190\\,{e}^{2.07} \\\\  & ≈12\\,547,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest whole number. \n\nTherefore, approximately $12\\,547$ fish will be in the pond after $23$ weeks." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-339239/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aeeaf85-0cbd-58ab-91d6-93448ff54b4d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-339239"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-339235/selection/7faf6f53ba78fcb1ae1e60fb39c421ee003772b21e9b2375481065d82c258f33" :answer/id #uuid "d663a389-a655-5127-b26c-cf28c23a6b89" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "242\\,650" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339235/selection/078379d4ecaf63b8f61ffcc0477a7320c71695a6cbddafad271e8dc32c5de293" :answer/id #uuid "64e5001b-e2fc-5260-88f6-41ffc5b29955" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "422\\,645" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339235/selection/ea472e9e08e59c0f3bd27c6e8e803c7fccd6065799342c67fb3457632e1d7b12" :answer/id #uuid "a7a20913-318d-5126-9e01-643eb8b57bf7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "242\\,506" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339235/selection/b924c37a9d285c4ce810a0f4c6fc31c84724345842cdf9b70e25037829ed6883" :answer/id #uuid "59f29b8a-2406-517e-b5b8-8b3e947655d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "422\\,564" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339235/selection/2403ed2abc647a34f211d646ddbd2e06cbd1b93778c60ba5661580429869e1a8" :answer/id #uuid "0e8cbef8-dd76-5ce2-9ea3-58c511c41843" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "224\\,605" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339235/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "058f8cd9-9c9a-563e-a3fc-6523a78e7be8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-339235/selection/2403ed2abc647a34f211d646ddbd2e06cbd1b93778c60ba5661580429869e1a8" :answer-field/choices ["q-339235/selection/7faf6f53ba78fcb1ae1e60fb39c421ee003772b21e9b2375481065d82c258f33" "q-339235/selection/078379d4ecaf63b8f61ffcc0477a7320c71695a6cbddafad271e8dc32c5de293" "q-339235/selection/ea472e9e08e59c0f3bd27c6e8e803c7fccd6065799342c67fb3457632e1d7b12" "q-339235/selection/b924c37a9d285c4ce810a0f4c6fc31c84724345842cdf9b70e25037829ed6883" "q-339235/selection/2403ed2abc647a34f211d646ddbd2e06cbd1b93778c60ba5661580429869e1a8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339235" :question/id #uuid "23693440-999a-50e6-bfda-ddb3bd32fa62" :question/math-academy-id "q-339235" :question/problem "The number of subscribers $S(t)$ to a new video streaming service after $t$ weeks can be modeled by the differential equation ${S}^{′}(t)=0.11S(t).$ If the streaming service had $60\\,000$ subscribers after $20$ weeks, calculate the number of subscribers after $32$ weeks." :question/worked-solution "The general solution to the given differential equation is\n\n$$\nS(t)={S}_{0}\\,{e}^{0.11t},\n$$\n\nwhere ${S}_{0}$ is the initial number of subscribers.\n\nWe are given that after $20$ weeks, $60\\,000$ people subscribed to the service. So, substituting $t=20$ and $S(20)=60\\,000$ into our general solution and solving for ${S}_{0},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S(20) & ={S}_{0}\\,{e}^{0.11\\cdot 20} \\\\ 60\\,000 & ={S}_{0}\\,{e}^{2.2} \\\\ {S}_{0} & =\\frac{60\\,000}{{e}^{2.2}} \\\\  & ≈6\\,648.190,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.\n\nHence, our particular solution is\n\n$$\nS(t)=6\\,648.190\\,{e}^{0.11t}.\n$$\n\nWe want to find the number of subscribers after $32$ weeks. So, substituting $t=32$ into our particular solution, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S(32) & =6\\,648.190\\,{e}^{0.11\\cdot 32} \\\\  & =6\\,648.190\\,{e}^{3.52} \\\\  & ≈224\\,605,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest whole number. \n\nTherefore, the streaming service will have about $224\\,605$ subscribers after $32$ weeks." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-339235/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aeeaf85-0cbd-58ab-91d6-93448ff54b4d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-339235"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-339248/selection/4eedbfdc290463fee0ee3c9157001af71c12c50e82647ff7736d16e412148eab" :answer/id #uuid "921b5e26-ac50-5182-b803-8acf97d7c381" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$31.13$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339248/selection/a267dcb583f9f1a4a1862d08c7f8c4a48304b8f163fcb22f7e162e8b87d705d0" :answer/id #uuid "196b8bc5-f372-5676-a6e7-e98af420b532" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$122.03$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339248/selection/d185a43d2ab1c6dd371edadd5f0f2f4e5bf8cad11a5416330006db3c5717fe74" :answer/id #uuid "a850e578-cba5-5daf-9d0e-c47606e88b88" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$114.93$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339248/selection/b328c5ca088d649b3aee12511bb0c19f516b5d9b20f2091c0b7d390870d9380f" :answer/id #uuid "add65ded-36d4-522b-8ca0-ebf3ee64d7c8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$113.25$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339248/selection/6814567c39a0962bf0f2a5f9f1a0c57cd18e6b891ab4a6d038384af667201028" :answer/id #uuid "9c248927-cf87-5799-a64a-2af0d4b12e4d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$116.01$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339248/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bd14324e-4b95-551f-bc7a-3003dd9bbfe2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-339248/selection/d185a43d2ab1c6dd371edadd5f0f2f4e5bf8cad11a5416330006db3c5717fe74" :answer-field/choices ["q-339248/selection/4eedbfdc290463fee0ee3c9157001af71c12c50e82647ff7736d16e412148eab" "q-339248/selection/a267dcb583f9f1a4a1862d08c7f8c4a48304b8f163fcb22f7e162e8b87d705d0" "q-339248/selection/d185a43d2ab1c6dd371edadd5f0f2f4e5bf8cad11a5416330006db3c5717fe74" "q-339248/selection/b328c5ca088d649b3aee12511bb0c19f516b5d9b20f2091c0b7d390870d9380f" "q-339248/selection/6814567c39a0962bf0f2a5f9f1a0c57cd18e6b891ab4a6d038384af667201028"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339248" :question/id #uuid "d1d42a16-3984-5dae-bf8b-539545f414f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-339248" :question/problem "The rate of increase ${E}^{′}(t)$ of the average monthly cost of electricity in a particular region varies according to the differential equation ${E}^{′}(t)=0.02E(t),$ where $t$ is the time, in years, since the year $2017.$ In $2021,$ the average monthly cost was $$124.50.$ What was the average monthly cost of electricity in $2017?$" :question/worked-solution "The general solution to the given differential equation is\n\n$$\nE(t)={E}_{0}\\,{e}^{0.02t},\n$$\n\nwhere ${E}_{0}$ is the average monthly cost of electricity in $2017.$\n\nWe are given that the monthly residential electricity cost was $$124.50$ in $2021,$ so after $t=4$ years. Hence, substituting $t=4$ and $E(4)=124.50$ into our general solution and solving for ${E}_{0},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}E(4) & ={E}_{0}\\,{e}^{0.02\\cdot 4} \\\\ 124.50 & ={E}_{0}\\,{e}^{0.08} \\\\ {E}_{0} & =\\frac{124.50}{{e}^{0.08}} \\\\  & ≈114.93\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest cent.\n\nTherefore, the average monthly cost in $2017$ was $$114.93.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-339248/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aeeaf85-0cbd-58ab-91d6-93448ff54b4d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-339248"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-339238/selection/eee15c9e72dfa9f80171bbed975c0ca489e66376a7c005c0cd2602e300cf797b" :answer/id #uuid "53f7a2c2-d01f-5d8d-bcd1-de3c18ef4cb8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$64\\,677$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339238/selection/7fc54e1a6d00a30f7e8feec12f6461826bb0a3616a9283d07840d1a970432f9f" :answer/id #uuid "e01eb0e1-30ca-55fa-adf9-dba1080fe548" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$74\\,744$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339238/selection/84eee32fcf15b0d3ae95abbfaefdb0cec41ff123cdfdbc594a8194d1048b5357" :answer/id #uuid "330284a9-1307-51b9-bc27-a76b6d784343" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$67\\,464$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339238/selection/845f5cb6f1cf26bc4f7a5e66c32f875136e143c1c2b6fb61c7b2537e1deca5f1" :answer/id #uuid "cd33aa87-e87a-5d59-b9b0-355900cc6177" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$77\\,644$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339238/selection/3746d7bdbd95ee90d6701949ed0934e68a8b4a6ac99d0062fbb094187c623c3d" :answer/id #uuid "22728bad-3dbc-567d-8f27-fe91043563fe" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$67\\,644$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339238/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6fc72f4a-10e5-5f2f-bce7-de962d0a7018" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-339238/selection/845f5cb6f1cf26bc4f7a5e66c32f875136e143c1c2b6fb61c7b2537e1deca5f1" :answer-field/choices ["q-339238/selection/eee15c9e72dfa9f80171bbed975c0ca489e66376a7c005c0cd2602e300cf797b" "q-339238/selection/7fc54e1a6d00a30f7e8feec12f6461826bb0a3616a9283d07840d1a970432f9f" "q-339238/selection/84eee32fcf15b0d3ae95abbfaefdb0cec41ff123cdfdbc594a8194d1048b5357" "q-339238/selection/845f5cb6f1cf26bc4f7a5e66c32f875136e143c1c2b6fb61c7b2537e1deca5f1" "q-339238/selection/3746d7bdbd95ee90d6701949ed0934e68a8b4a6ac99d0062fbb094187c623c3d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339238" :question/id #uuid "9b820df1-e416-5208-8973-cc88329588d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-339238" :question/problem "The value $P(t)$ of a particular luxury car $t$ years after the year $2010$ can be modeled by the differential equation ${P}^{′}(t)=0.025P(t).$ If the car's value in $2016$ was $$62\\,000,$ calculate its value in the year $2025.$" :question/worked-solution "The general solution to the given differential equation is\n\n$$\nP(t)={P}_{0}\\,{e}^{0.025t},\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{0}$ is the initial value of the car.\n\nWe are given that the value in $2016$ was $$62\\,000.$ So, substituting $t=6$ and $P(6)=$62\\,000$ into our general solution and solving for ${P}_{0},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(6) & ={P}_{0}\\,{e}^{0.025\\cdot 6} \\\\ 62\\,000 & ={P}_{0}\\,{e}^{0.15} \\\\ {P}_{0} & =\\frac{62\\,000}{{e}^{0.15}} \\\\  & ≈53\\,363.895,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.\n\nHence, our particular solution is\n\n$$\nP(t)=53\\,363.895\\,{e}^{0.025t}.\n$$\n\nWe want to find the car's value $15$ years after $2010.$ So, substituting $t=15$ into our particular solution, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(15) & =53\\,363.895\\,{e}^{0.025\\cdot 15} \\\\  & =53\\,363.895\\,{e}^{0.375} \\\\  & ≈77\\,644,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest whole number. \n\nTherefore, the car's value in $2025$ will be $$77\\,644.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-339238/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aeeaf85-0cbd-58ab-91d6-93448ff54b4d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-339238"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-21814"] :question/problem "The rate at which the balance in a savings account grows $B(t),$ after $t$ years, can be modeled by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d B}{\\textrm d t} = 0.05B.\n$$\n\nHow many years does it take for the balance to increase by $60\\%?$  Round your answer to the nearest year." :question/worked-solution "We model the balance growth using the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d B}{\\textrm d t} = 0.05B.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nB(t) = B_0\\,e^{0.05t},\n$$\n\nwhere $B_0$ is the initial balance.\n\nLet $t_1$ be the time when the balance has increased by $60\\%.$ That is,\n\n$$\nB(t_1) = 1.6B_0.\n$$\n\nWe solve the above equation for $t_1,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B({t}_{1}) & ={B}_{0}{e}^{0.05\\cdot {t}_{1}} \\\\ 1.6{B}_{0} & ={B}_{0}{e}^{0.05{t}_{1}} \\\\ 1.6 & ={e}^{0.05{t}_{1}} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(1.6) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{0.05{t}_{1}}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(1.6) & =0.05{t}_{1} \\\\ {t}_{1} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1.6)}{0.05} \\\\ {t}_{1} & ≈9.40\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRounding to the nearest integer, we conclude that it takes $9$ years for the balance to increase by $60\\%.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-21815"] :question/problem "The rate at which the amount of medicine in a person’s bloodstream decreases $M(t),$ after $t$ hours, can be modeled by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}M}{\\textrm{d}t} = -0.08M.\n$$\n\nHow many hours does it take for the amount of medicine to decrease to $30\\%$ of the original amount?  Round your answer to the nearest hour." :question/worked-solution "We model the amount of medicine using the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}M}{\\textrm{d}t} = -0.08M.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nM(t) = M_0\\,e^{-0.08t},\n$$\n\nwhere $M_0$ is the initial amount of medicine.\n\nLet $t_1$ be the time when the amount of medicine is $30\\%$ of the original amount. That is,\n\n$$\nM(t_1) = 0.30M_0.\n$$\n\nWe solve the above equation for $t_1,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.30{M}_{0} & ={M}_{0}\\,{e}^{-0.08{t}_{1}} \\\\ 0.30 & ={e}^{-0.08{t}_{1}} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.30) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{-0.08{t}_{1}}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.30) & =-0.08{t}_{1} \\\\ {t}_{1} & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.30)}{0.08} \\\\ {t}_{1} & ≈15.050\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRounding to the nearest integer, we conclude that it takes $15$ hours for the amount of medicine to decrease to $30\\%$ of the original amount." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-21816"] :question/problem "During an experiment, the weight $W(t)$ of an object varies according to the differential equation $W'(t) = -r W(t),$ where $t$ is the time, measured in hours, and $r > 0.$ It is known that the object's weight reduces by three-quarters after the first two hours. How long does it take for the object's weight to reduce to one-sixth of its original weight? Round your answer to one decimal place." :question/worked-solution "The general solution to the given differential equation is\n\n$$\nW(t) = W_0 e^{-rt},\n$$\n\nwhere $W_0$ is the weight when $t=0.$\n\nLet $t_1$ be the time when the weight equals $\\dfrac{1}{6}W_0.$ Then, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W({t}_{1}) & =\\frac{1}{6}{W}_{0}\\,⇒\\,{W}_{0}{e}^{-r{t}_{1}}=\\frac{1}{6}{W}_{0}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation for $t_1,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{W}_{0}{e}^{-r{t}_{1}} & =\\frac{1}{6}{W}_{0} \\\\ \\cancel{{W}_{0}}{e}^{-r{t}_{1}} & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cancel{{W}_{0}} \\\\ {e}^{-r{t}_{1}} & =\\frac{1}{6} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{-r{t}_{1}}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{6}) \\\\ -r{t}_{1} & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡6 \\\\ {t}_{1} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡6}{r}\\,\\,(∗)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now need to calculate $r.$ We're told that the weight reduces by three-quarters after the first two hours. Therefore, one-quarter of the weight remains, and we have\n\n$$\nW(2) = \\dfrac{1}{4}W_0\\quad \\Rightarrow\\quad W_0e^{-2r} = \\dfrac{1}{4}W_0\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation for $r,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{W}_{0}{e}^{-2r} & =\\frac{1}{4}{W}_{0} \\\\ \\cancel{{W}_{0}}{e}^{-2r} & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cancel{{W}_{0}} \\\\ {e}^{-2r} & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{-2r}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\ -2r & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4 \\\\ r & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4 \\\\ r & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡{4}^{1/2} \\\\ r & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting this into $(*)$ and evaluating, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}_{1} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡6}{r} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡6}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\  & ≈2.6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to one decimal place. \n\nTherefore, we conclude that it takes approximately $2.6$ hours for the weight to reduce to one-sixth of its original weight." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-21817"] :question/problem "A marathon runner is participating in a race. The remaining distance $D(t)$ they have left to run $t$ hours since starting the race can be modeled by the differential equation $D'(t)= -0.8D(t).$ Two hours into the race, they have $6\\,\\text{km}$ remaining. Calculate the distance remaining after four hours." :question/worked-solution "The general solution to the given differential equation is\n\n$$\nD(t) = D_0\\,e^{-0.8t},\n$$\n\nwhere $D_0$ is the remaining distance when $t=0.$\n\nWe are given that the remaining distance was $6\\,\\text{km}$ after $2$ hours. So, substituting $t=2$ and $D(2)=6$ into our general solution and solving for $D_0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(2) & ={D}_{0}\\,{e}^{-0.8\\cdot 2} \\\\ 6 & ={D}_{0}\\,{e}^{-1.6} \\\\ {D}_{0} & =\\frac{6}{{e}^{-1.6}} \\\\  & ≈29.718,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.\n\nHence, our particular solution is\n\n$$\nD(t) = 29.718\\,e^{-0.8t}.\n$$\n\nWe want to find the distance remaining after $4$ hours. So, substituting $t=4$ into our particular solution, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(4) & =29.718\\,{e}^{-0.8\\cdot 4} \\\\  & =29.718\\,{e}^{-3.2} \\\\  & ≈1.2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to one decimal place.\n\nTherefore, the remaining distance after $4$ hours is $1.2\\,\\text{km}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
